01:29:23.933 --> 01:29:26.482
But then stunts also includes cars

01:29:26.482 --> 01:29:28.927
you know, boats getting set on fire.

01:29:28.927 --> 01:29:30.221
- Yeah.

01:29:30.221 --> 01:29:31.865
- People, some stunt man have to like

01:29:31.865 --> 01:29:33.257
flip the cars over while they're innit.

01:29:33.257 --> 01:29:34.201
Which is just like.

01:29:34.201 --> 01:29:36.054
- That's a whole new skill set right.

01:29:36.054 --> 01:29:38.008
So It really like, you know,

01:29:38.008 --> 01:29:39.159
it's saying, what about stunts?

01:29:39.159 --> 01:29:40.639
It's kinda like saying how
long is a piece of string?

01:29:40.639 --> 01:29:42.125
There's so many different
things you can do.

01:29:42.125 --> 01:29:43.652
You can be like falling
off buildings and things.

01:29:43.652 --> 01:29:44.922
- So what was like some
of the stuff that you did?

01:29:44.922 --> 01:29:47.904
- So for me, I was doing
fight scenes, right?

01:29:47.904 --> 01:29:51.718
So like I trained in the
Hong Kong style of action

01:29:51.718 --> 01:29:54.461
and my master, I shouldn't call my master,

01:29:54.461 --> 01:29:56.155
the guy who was training me.

01:29:56.155 --> 01:29:58.213
He was on Jackie Chan's stunt team

01:29:58.213 --> 01:30:00.640
throughout the nineties and naughties.

01:30:00.640 --> 01:30:01.509
So he did movies like

01:30:01.509 --> 01:30:02.999
he did a couple of the Rush Hours.

01:30:02.999 --> 01:30:04.116
He did Shanghai Noon.

01:30:04.116 --> 01:30:04.949
- Oh wow.

01:30:04.949 --> 01:30:05.929
- He did some of the
smaller Hong Kong ones.

01:30:05.929 --> 01:30:09.499
Like the Twins Effect,
these kind of movies, right?

01:30:09.499 --> 01:30:13.722
But like the way they
work in Hong Kong is like

01:30:13.722 --> 01:30:16.723
I should stop saying like so
much, that's not good is it?

01:30:16.723 --> 01:30:18.165
- You say it less than us.

01:30:18.165 --> 01:30:22.039
- The way they like, oh
my God I did it again.

01:30:22.039 --> 01:30:24.042
The attitude, okay.

01:30:24.042 --> 01:30:27.640
The slogan of the Hong
Kong stuntman association

01:30:27.640 --> 01:30:32.212
he told me when he was in
it, risk life save money.

01:30:32.212 --> 01:30:33.240
So that's the kind of
attitude you're dealing with.

01:30:33.240 --> 01:30:34.838
- Wow.
- No bullshit.

01:30:34.838 --> 01:30:38.437
- If you, Dude I have never had
a harder teacher in my life.

01:30:38.437 --> 01:30:40.600
This dude was so tough.

01:30:40.600 --> 01:30:43.811
It's like, you're expected
to back flip off a balcony

01:30:43.811 --> 01:30:46.268
whilst on fire into a
pool of broken glass.

01:30:46.268 --> 01:30:48.447
And if you're like a little bit hesitant

01:30:48.447 --> 01:30:51.889
he's like, No, No. You're so weak.

01:30:51.889 --> 01:30:54.892
What's wrong with you?
Harden up. Harden up.

01:30:54.892 --> 01:30:57.206
- That is the ultimate Chad.

01:30:57.206 --> 01:31:00.024
- It's just like a psychopath.

01:31:00.024 --> 01:31:04.945
- But the stunts attracts
kind of type A personality.

01:31:04.945 --> 01:31:06.401
- Yeah.

01:31:06.401 --> 01:31:08.716
- He was like, he was
telling me stories about when

01:31:08.716 --> 01:31:11.446
he was back in Australia
he was from Melbourne.

01:31:11.446 --> 01:31:14.670
In Australia before he went
to Hong Kong was with Jackie.

01:31:14.670 --> 01:31:19.231
Just the stuff he did just as
a thing to do, was bonkers.

01:31:19.231 --> 01:31:20.676
- What, like as a hobby?

01:31:20.676 --> 01:31:21.950
- No, it's a hobby but like,

01:31:21.950 --> 01:31:24.372
you kind of do it towards stunts sort of,

01:31:24.372 --> 01:31:25.445
but he was like one day

01:31:25.445 --> 01:31:29.292
we were driving past a
train station in Melbourne.

01:31:29.292 --> 01:31:30.977
And you know, there's like the bridge

01:31:30.977 --> 01:31:32.797
that goes over the train tracks.

01:31:32.797 --> 01:31:34.611
And then there's like a pole sticking up

01:31:34.611 --> 01:31:36.876
like 10 meters away from it or something.

01:31:36.876 --> 01:31:39.225
A pole with the dingy dongy
lights on it or something.

01:31:39.225 --> 01:31:40.517
And he was like,

01:31:40.517 --> 01:31:42.694
yeah so when I was younger,
before I went to Hong Kong

01:31:42.694 --> 01:31:45.136
I was gonna jump off the
bridge onto the pole.

01:31:45.136 --> 01:31:46.194
Yeah. I was gonna do that.

01:31:46.194 --> 01:31:49.127
Yeah. We didn't have a camera at the time.

01:31:49.127 --> 01:31:50.415
I'm like, what?

01:31:50.415 --> 01:31:52.498
You know, jump off. What?

01:31:53.508 --> 01:31:54.341
- Just for fun?

01:31:54.341 --> 01:31:56.062
- Just telling me to jump from this bridge

01:31:56.062 --> 01:31:59.054
onto catch a pole, just yeah.

01:31:59.054 --> 01:32:00.971
- To be like, I did it.

01:32:01.937 --> 01:32:03.120
- Here's a thing to do.

01:32:03.120 --> 01:32:04.876
I think his attitude was he would film it

01:32:04.876 --> 01:32:07.602
and it will become part
of his stunt show reel.

01:32:07.602 --> 01:32:09.215
I think that was his attitude.

01:32:09.215 --> 01:32:10.569
But that's the kind of people like,

01:32:10.569 --> 01:32:11.468
just fearless men.

01:32:11.468 --> 01:32:12.701
- So you're doing stupid shit,

01:32:12.701 --> 01:32:16.231
like jumping off
buildings into like glass?

01:32:16.231 --> 01:32:17.064
Where do you draw the line?

01:32:17.064 --> 01:32:18.815
- I didn't. Cause I'm not that talented.

01:32:18.815 --> 01:32:19.856
Other people-
- Talented?

01:32:19.856 --> 01:32:21.601
- What talents you need?

01:32:21.601 --> 01:32:22.580
I mean, like, how do you train for them?

01:32:22.580 --> 01:32:23.627
That's what I wanna know.

01:32:23.627 --> 01:32:26.299
- There's a natural level
of talent that's required.

01:32:26.299 --> 01:32:27.700
So the guys who become a career stuntmen

01:32:27.700 --> 01:32:29.753
generally speaking, the
kids who were, you know

01:32:29.753 --> 01:32:30.941
the fastest runners in school.

01:32:30.941 --> 01:32:34.666
The kids who had naturally
very physically active.

01:32:34.666 --> 01:32:36.221
I'm not I was a fat kid at school.

01:32:36.221 --> 01:32:37.977
So I've got a level of
skill just cause I trained

01:32:37.977 --> 01:32:39.791
but I don't have the
natural talent for it.

01:32:39.791 --> 01:32:40.624
- Right.

01:32:40.624 --> 01:32:42.701
- These guys, man, like
I've got friends who now

01:32:42.701 --> 01:32:44.460
are doing the stunts in all the,

01:32:44.460 --> 01:32:46.657
like the Marvel films or so forth.

01:32:46.657 --> 01:32:48.468
And they're just,

01:32:48.468 --> 01:32:50.494
the moment they were born,

01:32:50.494 --> 01:32:51.603
they were better than me

01:32:51.603 --> 01:32:53.782
after a hundred years of training,
you know what I'm saying?

01:32:53.782 --> 01:32:55.354
It's like my Capoeira teacher.

01:32:55.354 --> 01:32:56.872
- That guy throw himself off buildings

01:32:56.872 --> 01:32:59.130
so goddamn good. I wish that were me.

01:32:59.130 --> 01:33:03.262
- It's like they back
flipped out of the womb

01:33:03.262 --> 01:33:04.836
with a six pack.

01:33:04.836 --> 01:33:07.479
And a charming smile, you know.

01:33:07.479 --> 01:33:09.826
It's just ridiculous.

01:33:09.826 --> 01:33:11.169
Like, goodness.

01:33:11.169 --> 01:33:12.002
Yeah so it's like,

01:33:12.002 --> 01:33:14.174
that's the level of natural
talent that's required.

01:33:14.174 --> 01:33:15.208
But also when you get to that,

01:33:15.208 --> 01:33:18.375
a lot of them just type-A personality.

01:33:20.348 --> 01:33:23.260
- I mean you have to be,
you can't, you can't like.

01:33:23.260 --> 01:33:25.326
- If you're willing to
be hit by a car, you know

01:33:25.326 --> 01:33:27.704
like just stand there, we're
going to drive a car into you.

01:33:27.704 --> 01:33:28.537
Okay.

01:33:29.822 --> 01:33:31.179
You know, it's so frickin' crazy.

01:33:31.179 --> 01:33:32.732
- Good take, good take.

01:33:32.732 --> 01:33:34.699
- Was it good? Was it good?
All right let's do it again.

01:33:34.699 --> 01:33:36.862
- Just on the ground legs
broken, is that good?

01:33:36.862 --> 01:33:38.427
- A lot of wrestlers as well.

01:33:38.427 --> 01:33:39.716
It's like, you know, okay.

01:33:39.716 --> 01:33:40.914
It's funny. When you're pro wrestlers,

01:33:40.914 --> 01:33:42.817
you're backstage in the locker room.

01:33:42.817 --> 01:33:44.668
Everyone's normally so mellow.

01:33:44.668 --> 01:33:46.418
It was just like, Oh.

01:33:48.458 --> 01:33:50.226
So chilled out.

01:33:50.226 --> 01:33:52.532
And then, okay, so we'll go onto the ring

01:33:52.532 --> 01:33:54.993
and three minutes in or so

01:33:54.993 --> 01:33:58.076
you can hit me with the baseball bat.

01:33:59.092 --> 01:34:01.017
Wrap up a barbed wire.

01:34:01.017 --> 01:34:03.083
He's like, hmm.

01:34:03.083 --> 01:34:04.523
They hit me with it here last week

01:34:04.523 --> 01:34:05.356
it's still healing.

01:34:05.356 --> 01:34:07.749
So you better hit me with it here.

01:34:07.749 --> 01:34:08.696
Really? Are you sure?

01:34:08.696 --> 01:34:10.401
That's what you want me to do?

01:34:10.401 --> 01:34:12.330
Let's take a quick break
for this one minute break.

01:34:12.330 --> 01:34:13.688
And we'll be right back

01:34:13.688 --> 01:34:15.795
on the voice of Africa radio network.

01:34:15.795 --> 01:34:17.613
- It's funny because wrestlers will be

01:34:17.613 --> 01:34:21.455
in the locker room and they all Oh, Oh,

01:34:21.455 --> 01:34:24.372
they're taping up knees and things.

01:34:25.710 --> 01:34:27.585
They go out to the ring and it's.

01:34:27.585 --> 01:34:29.483
And they're superheroes, right?

01:34:29.483 --> 01:34:31.678
They go back, they're all
bleeding and everything.

01:34:31.678 --> 01:34:33.095
Blood everywhere.

01:34:36.942 --> 01:34:38.913
Stunt people and pro wrestlers,

01:34:38.913 --> 01:34:40.330
it's what a life.

01:34:41.806 --> 01:34:43.188
- What a life.

01:34:43.188 --> 01:34:44.233
- What a life eh?

01:34:44.233 --> 01:34:45.501
- Credits roll.

01:34:45.501 --> 01:34:46.882
- What a gimmick.

01:34:46.882 --> 01:34:48.409
- I mean, I suppose like

01:34:48.409 --> 01:34:51.113
pro wrestlers is just a natural
evolution of stuntmen right?

01:34:51.113 --> 01:34:53.458
Because it's just like,
it's more controlled stunts

01:34:53.458 --> 01:34:54.989
and you add a narrative to it.

01:34:54.989 --> 01:34:55.822
- I felt that way.

01:34:55.822 --> 01:34:58.005
And also the guys who tend go into stunts

01:34:58.005 --> 01:34:59.817
tend to be much more like
talented with the physical stuff.

01:34:59.817 --> 01:35:01.995
And I was better at the
character performance type stuff.

01:35:01.995 --> 01:35:05.107
So for me it seemed like a
much more natural evolution.

01:35:05.107 --> 01:35:09.007
- What are some of the craziest
stunts you've had to do?

01:35:09.007 --> 01:35:09.992
- Well, I wasn't that good.

01:35:09.992 --> 01:35:12.539
So I didn't get to do
that much amazing stuff.

01:35:12.539 --> 01:35:14.835
Jumping off balconies done some of that.

01:35:14.835 --> 01:35:16.916
It's not that hard.

01:35:16.916 --> 01:35:18.040
- I mean, I, I dunno.

01:35:18.040 --> 01:35:21.120
I wouldn't want to jump
off a balcony personally.

01:35:21.120 --> 01:35:22.230
- How tall are we talking here?

01:35:22.230 --> 01:35:23.563
- Not that tall.

01:35:24.596 --> 01:35:25.711
Second story.

01:35:25.711 --> 01:35:27.044
- What the fuck.

01:35:28.397 --> 01:35:30.717
- It's still pretty
tall. I wouldn't do it.

01:35:30.717 --> 01:35:34.785
- My trainer was like, you're
weak, you're such a sissy.

01:35:34.785 --> 01:35:37.538
He's doing like 20 stories
and things, you know.

01:35:37.538 --> 01:35:38.702
Just insane.

01:35:38.702 --> 01:35:40.356
- This is how real Chad does it.

01:35:40.356 --> 01:35:41.803
- Oh my God, man.

01:35:41.803 --> 01:35:43.082
It was never good enough.

01:35:43.082 --> 01:35:45.188
- Some people are just
like cockroaches right?

01:35:45.188 --> 01:35:47.611
They just can't die.

01:35:47.611 --> 01:35:49.770
- Honestly, honestly.
- Like honestly.

01:35:49.770 --> 01:35:51.207
- In pro wrestling a hit over the head

01:35:51.207 --> 01:35:53.642
with one of those fluorescent light tubes.

01:35:53.642 --> 01:35:54.885
That was good. That actually doesn't hurt,

01:35:54.885 --> 01:35:56.126
but it does cut you.

01:35:56.126 --> 01:35:57.959
So we end up bleeding.

01:35:59.802 --> 01:36:02.111
- Have you ever gotten
injured or anything like that?

01:36:02.111 --> 01:36:04.390
- Like properly injured.

01:36:04.390 --> 01:36:07.177
- Well I probably been
concussed, but didn't realize.

01:36:07.177 --> 01:36:08.421
You know what I'm saying?

01:36:08.421 --> 01:36:09.720
- How do you not realize.

01:36:09.720 --> 01:36:11.526
- I don't know what you're
saying, unfortunately.

01:36:11.526 --> 01:36:13.582
- If I get concussed, I
immediately realize it.

01:36:13.582 --> 01:36:14.656
- Do you really though?

01:36:14.656 --> 01:36:15.735
That's the thing about concussion.

01:36:15.735 --> 01:36:16.972
You don't know what's going on.

01:36:16.972 --> 01:36:17.844
That's a whole thing about concussion,

01:36:17.844 --> 01:36:18.793
you don't know what's going on.

01:36:18.793 --> 01:36:20.229
So you need someone to stop you

01:36:20.229 --> 01:36:21.737
and be like, you're concussed.

01:36:21.737 --> 01:36:24.184
We need to do the whatever
happens after concussions.

01:36:24.184 --> 01:36:27.103
We do what people who've
done a first aid course.

01:36:27.103 --> 01:36:28.418
- It's like people who
play American football

01:36:28.418 --> 01:36:29.742
like never know that they're concussed.

01:36:29.742 --> 01:36:31.344
- Yeah, exactly. They go
back straight to the field.

01:36:31.344 --> 01:36:32.177
- Oh geez.

01:36:32.177 --> 01:36:33.796
- I think it's like
they have like the most,

01:36:33.796 --> 01:36:34.629
I think they die early

01:36:34.629 --> 01:36:36.266
cause they have so much brain damage.

01:36:36.266 --> 01:36:37.749
They're just hitting
their head constantly.

01:36:37.749 --> 01:36:38.654
But they don't know.

01:36:38.654 --> 01:36:40.348
- So it's the same with MMA fighters

01:36:40.348 --> 01:36:41.704
in training just getting jabbed,

01:36:41.704 --> 01:36:42.648
just getting little punches.

01:36:42.648 --> 01:36:44.962
They get like compounded
brain damage from that.

01:36:44.962 --> 01:36:46.327
It's not from getting knocked out.

01:36:46.327 --> 01:36:48.880
It's just from little shots over.

01:36:48.880 --> 01:36:51.347
Anyway, so light over the head,

01:36:51.347 --> 01:36:52.602
broken glass.

01:36:52.602 --> 01:36:53.536
Sorry, not broken glass.

01:36:53.536 --> 01:36:55.467
Barbed wire did some of that.

01:36:55.467 --> 01:36:57.300
- You look like Jesus?

01:36:59.169 --> 01:37:00.606
- Hit with a shovel.

01:37:00.606 --> 01:37:01.646
I got hit in the head with a shovel.

01:37:01.646 --> 01:37:02.940
- You got hit in the head with a shovel?

01:37:02.940 --> 01:37:04.160
- It was a great weapon.

01:37:04.160 --> 01:37:05.564
- Like how hard are we talking?

01:37:05.564 --> 01:37:08.751
Like just like a little like boop or?

01:37:08.751 --> 01:37:09.626
- Bonked!

01:37:09.626 --> 01:37:10.620
- Oh fuck.
- It was a great weapon.

01:37:10.620 --> 01:37:12.071
But if you hit it with the concave side,

01:37:12.071 --> 01:37:13.474
it's not that bad on your skull.

01:37:13.474 --> 01:37:15.081
The convex side would really mess you up.

01:37:15.081 --> 01:37:17.178
The concave side, you know,
folds onto your skull.

01:37:17.178 --> 01:37:18.381
- Right, right.

01:37:18.381 --> 01:37:19.709
But like to control that right,

01:37:19.709 --> 01:37:20.987
in the swing, would it be

01:37:20.987 --> 01:37:22.498
I feel it's a lot harder than it looks.

01:37:22.498 --> 01:37:25.022
- Because like there's
a image in pro wrestling

01:37:25.022 --> 01:37:26.333
that you know, pro wrestling is fake

01:37:26.333 --> 01:37:27.166
and everything like that.

01:37:27.166 --> 01:37:28.338
But obviously the stunts are real.

01:37:28.338 --> 01:37:30.639
Like how hard you have
to go for the stunts

01:37:30.639 --> 01:37:32.776
that you do in pro wrestling?

01:37:32.776 --> 01:37:33.690
- Well, it depends.

01:37:33.690 --> 01:37:37.523
It depends on you, I
mean give it hell really.

01:37:38.435 --> 01:37:39.669
- So when you're saying the shovel right?

01:37:39.669 --> 01:37:41.532
In my mind my immediate thought is,

01:37:41.532 --> 01:37:42.571
guy swing shovel

01:37:42.571 --> 01:37:44.884
tries his best to stop
it, but it still hits you.

01:37:44.884 --> 01:37:45.717
Is that what's happening?

01:37:45.717 --> 01:37:47.117
Or is he literally going, like,

01:37:47.117 --> 01:37:47.950
I'm gonna hit you with the shovel.

01:37:47.950 --> 01:37:50.112
- No. Hit me as hard as you can.

01:37:50.112 --> 01:37:51.230
- Why?
- What?

01:37:51.230 --> 01:37:52.685
- Cause I guess like,

01:37:52.685 --> 01:37:54.822
the audience needs to
hear the sound, right?

01:37:54.822 --> 01:37:55.655
- To hear the sound.

01:37:55.655 --> 01:37:57.415
And also it's you know, like just-

01:37:57.415 --> 01:37:59.745
- Get one of those soundboard in the back.

01:37:59.745 --> 01:38:02.301
- When you're wrestling,
you want to do it, you know

01:38:02.301 --> 01:38:05.088
there's an element of, come on, you know?

01:38:05.088 --> 01:38:05.921
- No I don't.

01:38:05.921 --> 01:38:08.827
That's why, that's why
I'm not a pro wrestler.

01:38:08.827 --> 01:38:10.147
I'm a virgin.

01:38:10.147 --> 01:38:12.508
This Chad versus the virgin.

01:38:12.508 --> 01:38:14.478
- I think you're making
anyone listening to this

01:38:14.478 --> 01:38:16.258
sound like virgin.

01:38:16.258 --> 01:38:18.428
Frankly, frankly I don't
want to be hit in the head

01:38:18.428 --> 01:38:19.628
with a shovel.

01:38:19.628 --> 01:38:20.631
- I used to love it.

01:38:20.631 --> 01:38:25.374
It's a young man's game,
it's a young man's game.

01:38:25.374 --> 01:38:28.200
- You're talking about this
like it's a past time, you know.

01:38:28.200 --> 01:38:30.170
- I feel like, why is it, you know,

01:38:30.170 --> 01:38:31.320
when a kid says that, it's like

01:38:31.320 --> 01:38:32.845
oh God, this kid is going nowhere.

01:38:32.845 --> 01:38:33.678
When an adult says it,

01:38:33.678 --> 01:38:36.651
wow, he's such a manly adult.

01:38:36.651 --> 01:38:40.353
I feel if my son comes up to me, age five,

01:38:40.353 --> 01:38:42.396
