01:48:32.064 --> 01:48:33.008
into it.

01:48:33.008 --> 01:48:34.902
And time is, I feel like the hardest find

01:48:34.902 --> 01:48:36.345
the hardest thing to find as an adult,

01:48:36.345 --> 01:48:38.644
because everyone I've talked
whose learned Japanese

01:48:38.644 --> 01:48:40.290
no matter what way they went through,

01:48:40.290 --> 01:48:41.608
what path they went through

01:48:41.608 --> 01:48:44.450
there's no getting around,
just putting the hours into it.

01:48:44.450 --> 01:48:47.558
And it's like difficult
in our situation because

01:48:47.558 --> 01:48:49.251
with our situation, you know,

01:48:49.251 --> 01:48:50.328
it's different from your situation.

01:48:50.328 --> 01:48:52.346
Cause we can, we can go about our day

01:48:52.346 --> 01:48:54.399
and just not speak any Japanese at all

01:48:54.399 --> 01:48:55.386
and be completely fine with it

01:48:55.386 --> 01:48:57.128
cause we work from home.

01:48:57.128 --> 01:48:58.399
So it goes down to having

01:48:58.399 --> 01:49:00.429
to find time outside of your schedule

01:49:00.429 --> 01:49:02.418
to like learn Japanese.

01:49:02.418 --> 01:49:04.108
- Cause I'm sure if Garnt and Connor

01:49:04.108 --> 01:49:06.657
were thrown into a situation where like,

01:49:06.657 --> 01:49:08.349
you're stuck in this village in Japan,

01:49:08.349 --> 01:49:10.322
when not a single person
can speak English.

01:49:10.322 --> 01:49:12.699
So you just have to get, you
know, make your way through it

01:49:12.699 --> 01:49:14.245
by trying to speak as
much Japanese as possible.

01:49:14.245 --> 01:49:16.505
I'm sure anybody in that
situation will be like,

01:49:16.505 --> 01:49:17.338
all right,

01:49:17.338 --> 01:49:18.614
I guess I've got to start
speaking Japanese, right?

01:49:18.614 --> 01:49:19.447
- That's one option.

01:49:19.447 --> 01:49:20.900
- It's unfortunate cause I mean,

01:49:20.900 --> 01:49:23.356
it's obviously great that
we have so much work to do

01:49:23.356 --> 01:49:26.886
and that, you know, it is
so successful cause you know

01:49:26.886 --> 01:49:29.222
I would love to take a year off

01:49:29.222 --> 01:49:30.958
and just do nothing and learn it.

01:49:30.958 --> 01:49:31.791
- I'd love to do that as well.

01:49:31.791 --> 01:49:34.420
- Unfortunately it makes
literally no sense right now

01:49:34.420 --> 01:49:37.628
to do that because you know,
everything's going so well.

01:49:37.628 --> 01:49:39.569
- I reckon if I had control your schedule

01:49:39.569 --> 01:49:44.097
I could get your Japanese
learning stuck in there.

01:49:44.097 --> 01:49:46.135
You've gotta be ruthless about it.

01:49:46.135 --> 01:49:48.257
You've gotta find little windows,

01:49:48.257 --> 01:49:51.308
little windows of time
where you can slip it in.

01:49:51.308 --> 01:49:54.316
And the things like first
thing in the morning.

01:49:54.316 --> 01:49:56.627
Yo get Peppa Pig dubbed into Japanese.

01:49:56.627 --> 01:49:58.228
I'm not joking. I'm not joking.

01:49:58.228 --> 01:50:00.287
That's great because you can see,

01:50:00.287 --> 01:50:03.222
the situations they're
going through are so basic.

01:50:03.222 --> 01:50:04.962
And every day, this is my mom.

01:50:04.962 --> 01:50:06.283
This is my dad.

01:50:06.283 --> 01:50:08.350
We're kicking a ball. You know.

01:50:08.350 --> 01:50:09.993
Go through that, that's
gonna teach you properly.

01:50:09.993 --> 01:50:11.224
Then also get your damn books

01:50:11.224 --> 01:50:13.368
and your teachers, and your class.

01:50:13.368 --> 01:50:15.285
- How many seasons were Peppa Pig?

01:50:15.285 --> 01:50:17.035
- It's not that many.

01:50:18.155 --> 01:50:20.046
- How long before you
started learning Japanese

01:50:20.046 --> 01:50:21.196
to the point where you
were like, all right,

01:50:21.196 --> 01:50:23.010
I'm pretty pretty fluent now.

01:50:23.010 --> 01:50:24.248
- Being in Japan,

01:50:24.248 --> 01:50:28.444
it was one year before I was
not a total moron anymore.

01:50:28.444 --> 01:50:31.669
Two years before I felt somewhat competent

01:50:31.669 --> 01:50:35.541
but I'd say five years before
I really feel like I can.

01:50:35.541 --> 01:50:36.989
- Talk to anyone, talk about anything.

01:50:36.989 --> 01:50:40.113
- I don't even really still
feel I can do that, you know.

01:50:40.113 --> 01:50:41.561
If I don't know someone,

01:50:41.561 --> 01:50:42.842
if they start doing something like weird

01:50:42.842 --> 01:50:46.288
like talking keigo, see
you later. I can't do that.

01:50:46.288 --> 01:50:47.722
See you later man.

01:50:47.722 --> 01:50:49.177
That's like a different language.

01:50:49.177 --> 01:50:50.863
Next stop they're pulling out Kansai-ben.

01:50:50.863 --> 01:50:53.088
I'm like, who's this jackass?

01:50:53.088 --> 01:50:55.589
What'd you do talking to
me like some Kansai person.

01:50:55.589 --> 01:50:57.646
- Oh yeah, I mean like you
know, keigo I guess is like,

01:50:57.646 --> 01:50:59.985
you know, everybody, everywhere in Japan

01:50:59.985 --> 01:51:01.947
you know, usually, you know, uses it.

01:51:01.947 --> 01:51:04.085
But when it comes to different dialects,

01:51:04.085 --> 01:51:07.528
like even I'm sometimes completely lost.

01:51:07.528 --> 01:51:08.570
- It's not very confidence inspiring

01:51:08.570 --> 01:51:09.855
when you talk to natives and they're like

01:51:09.855 --> 01:51:10.688
I don't know what they're saying.

01:51:10.688 --> 01:51:12.329
And I'm like, what the
fuck am I suppose say?

01:51:12.329 --> 01:51:13.364
- Like Kansai-ben right?

01:51:13.364 --> 01:51:14.720
It's like, because you hear it so much

01:51:14.720 --> 01:51:16.257
on TV and stuff like that.

01:51:16.257 --> 01:51:17.740
It's like one dialect
where I'm like, okay yeah.

01:51:17.740 --> 01:51:19.429
I can kind of figure
out what you're saying

01:51:19.429 --> 01:51:21.245
but if I'm in like, you know,

01:51:21.245 --> 01:51:26.153
Okinawa or like middle of
nowhere in Hokkaido all right?

01:51:26.153 --> 01:51:28.699
Then I'll be like, I think
you're speaking Japanese

01:51:28.699 --> 01:51:30.755
but I couldn't tell you
what the fuck you're saying.

01:51:30.755 --> 01:51:33.348
- Did you have to, so you
grew up speaking Japanese,

01:51:33.348 --> 01:51:35.229
but did you have, were
there parts of the language

01:51:35.229 --> 01:51:36.181
you needed to study?

01:51:36.181 --> 01:51:37.213
Like particles or anything like that?

01:51:37.213 --> 01:51:38.046
- Yeah, absolutely.

01:51:38.046 --> 01:51:40.546
So like I did the JLPT-
- Okay.

01:51:41.554 --> 01:51:45.033
- Which is like the Japanese
language proficiency test.

01:51:45.033 --> 01:51:48.059
And I got N1 which is the highest level

01:51:48.059 --> 01:51:49.231
I had to study for that.

01:51:49.231 --> 01:51:52.845
I got that when I was
like 14, I think 14, 15

01:51:52.845 --> 01:51:55.598
but I studied like fucking crazy for that.

01:51:55.598 --> 01:51:57.673
- Good man, see he studied.

01:51:57.673 --> 01:51:58.506
- That's the thing,

01:51:58.506 --> 01:52:00.163
people think that like, Oh, fluent people

01:52:00.163 --> 01:52:02.060
well you know, people who have
it as their first language

01:52:02.060 --> 01:52:03.838
have it easy because
you don't have to study.

01:52:03.838 --> 01:52:05.087
No, that's complete bullshit.

01:52:05.087 --> 01:52:06.973
You have to study just
as hard as everybody else

01:52:06.973 --> 01:52:08.181
if you want to get good at it.

01:52:08.181 --> 01:52:10.033
- Yeah. Cause the thing is you also,

01:52:10.033 --> 01:52:14.783
you said, you also said you
speak five languages as well.

01:52:15.809 --> 01:52:18.282
- Fluent in English.
Half-assed at another four.

01:52:18.282 --> 01:52:20.007
- What other four? What
other four do you speak?

01:52:20.007 --> 01:52:24.334
- So, Japanese Cantonese,
Mandarin, German.

01:52:24.334 --> 01:52:25.167
- German?

01:52:25.167 --> 01:52:26.399
- I learned German in high school.

01:52:26.399 --> 01:52:28.153
- Oh, okay.
- And you've remember it?

01:52:28.153 --> 01:52:30.050
- Yeah. But it's been,
but I haven't spoken it

01:52:30.050 --> 01:52:30.972
for a long time.

01:52:30.972 --> 01:52:32.458
I went there on exchange.

01:52:32.458 --> 01:52:35.488
So I got that native exposure.

01:52:35.488 --> 01:52:38.069
But now I'm just big time out of practice.

01:52:38.069 --> 01:52:40.172
So if I start trying to talk, I would need

01:52:40.172 --> 01:52:42.300
like if you dumped me at
a German village somewhere

01:52:42.300 --> 01:52:44.193
I'd get it back a month or two maybe.

01:52:44.193 --> 01:52:45.070
- Right.

01:52:45.070 --> 01:52:46.634
- But I need to go through remembering

01:52:46.634 --> 01:52:49.809
a lot of vocab, specific bits
of grammar, how it works.

01:52:49.809 --> 01:52:51.616
Interestingly German grammar
is not that different

01:52:51.616 --> 01:52:52.983
from Japanese grammar.

01:52:52.983 --> 01:52:55.239
- Yeah. A lot of Eastern
European languages actually

01:52:55.239 --> 01:52:56.612
are kind of similar to that you know.

01:52:56.612 --> 01:52:58.296
- Would you say that after you
learned your first language

01:52:58.296 --> 01:53:00.588
it was like way easier
to learn other languages?

01:53:00.588 --> 01:53:01.421
Cause that's what I've heard.

01:53:01.421 --> 01:53:02.254
- No.

01:53:03.107 --> 01:53:04.871
- See because I've heard
that's the thing like,

01:53:04.871 --> 01:53:08.218
I felt, cause my grandad
could speak seven languages.

01:53:08.218 --> 01:53:09.170
Fluently.

01:53:09.170 --> 01:53:11.836
- I think you just learn
what system works for you.

01:53:11.836 --> 01:53:12.871
- Yeah. Yeah.

01:53:12.871 --> 01:53:15.005
But like I also heard that like languages

01:53:15.005 --> 01:53:17.103
are a lot similar to instruments

01:53:17.103 --> 01:53:19.536
where the second one is always the hardest

01:53:19.536 --> 01:53:21.216
and then it gets easier and easier

01:53:21.216 --> 01:53:24.001
because you, every with
every new thing you learn,

01:53:24.001 --> 01:53:25.281
you use your base knowledge

01:53:25.281 --> 01:53:26.962
from the previous thing you've learned

01:53:26.962 --> 01:53:27.872
to kind of build upon it.

01:53:27.872 --> 01:53:30.005
So it was like, Oh, this is
a completely new language.

01:53:30.005 --> 01:53:32.146
But I already know a language that has

01:53:32.146 --> 01:53:34.486
kind of the same base sentence structure

01:53:34.486 --> 01:53:37.479
or same vocabulary rules as this one.

01:53:37.479 --> 01:53:39.419
- I have found that to mess me up.

01:53:39.419 --> 01:53:40.252
- Oh really?

01:53:40.252 --> 01:53:41.690
- Because now I'm just confused.

01:53:41.690 --> 01:53:43.474
Now I'm going into, let's say

01:53:43.474 --> 01:53:45.786
if I'm going from like
Japanese to Mandarin.

01:53:45.786 --> 01:53:48.459
Now I'm trying to do Mandarin grammar

01:53:48.459 --> 01:53:52.768
but I'm instinctively picking
Japanese words, right?

01:53:52.768 --> 01:53:55.487
Nod that head Ashley, good man.

01:53:55.487 --> 01:53:56.684
Ashley knows what's up.

01:53:56.684 --> 01:53:58.002
I imagined Shiori's nodding the head.

01:53:58.002 --> 01:53:59.335
I can't see her.

01:54:01.731 --> 01:54:04.112
So, so, but hang on.

01:54:04.112 --> 01:54:06.697
But you watch anime for
like a thousand hours a day.

01:54:06.697 --> 01:54:08.258
Surely something comes from that.

01:54:08.258 --> 01:54:09.785
- No, no. That's a fallacy.

01:54:09.785 --> 01:54:13.010
- I never, ever intended
to learn Japanese.

01:54:13.010 --> 01:54:15.477
When I was like, you know, 17, 18,

01:54:15.477 --> 01:54:18.851
I thought it's cringe to want
to learn Japanese from anime.

01:54:18.851 --> 01:54:21.649
- Look at this guy. HAHA.

01:54:21.649 --> 01:54:23.311
Tell me more.

01:54:23.311 --> 01:54:24.222
- Yeah, that's what I thought.

01:54:24.222 --> 01:54:25.055
And then now I'm like,

01:54:25.055 --> 01:54:27.775
fuck I'm such an idiot that
I thought it was cringe.

01:54:27.775 --> 01:54:30.566
- It was like looked down
upon in the anime community.

01:54:30.566 --> 01:54:31.763
Cause we had like the whole,

01:54:31.763 --> 01:54:33.361
the whole like weeaboo movement where-

01:54:33.361 --> 01:54:35.498
- Cause people will then start like trying

01:54:35.498 --> 01:54:37.238
to talk Japanese to you online.

01:54:37.238 --> 01:54:39.608
And it's like, what are
you doing? This is cringe.

01:54:39.608 --> 01:54:41.325
You know, they're not really
trying to learn the language.

01:54:41.325 --> 01:54:44.101
They're just trying to
learn a couple of phrases.

01:54:44.101 --> 01:54:46.617
- They just want to be like
their favorite anime characters.

01:54:46.617 --> 01:54:47.904
- Because let's be real like,

01:54:47.904 --> 01:54:49.754
the Japanese you hear in anime,

01:54:49.754 --> 01:54:52.461
like 99% of the time is not
the way Japanese people speak.

01:54:52.461 --> 01:54:53.408
- That's why you can't learn from it.

01:54:53.408 --> 01:54:54.241
- Right. Exactly.

01:54:54.241 --> 01:54:56.339
I mean, I mean, I think
you can learn from it

01:54:56.339 --> 01:54:58.020
but you shouldn't completely base

01:54:58.020 --> 01:54:59.128
all your knowledge off of it.

01:54:59.128 --> 01:54:59.961
- But it's a different level

01:54:59.961 --> 01:55:01.527
it's once you've already got your base

01:55:01.527 --> 01:55:03.425
you can talk about slaying dragons.

01:55:03.425 --> 01:55:06.207
- I would also say that
watching anime with subtitles

01:55:06.207 --> 01:55:08.668
is a wholly different
experience from watching anime

01:55:08.668 --> 01:55:11.752
to learn it because I've,
I've realized this now

01:55:11.752 --> 01:55:12.993
as I'm trying to learn Japanese,

01:55:12.993 --> 01:55:16.012
that the subtitles are just distracting.

01:55:16.012 --> 01:55:17.700
I think it's actually
worse to learn Japanese

01:55:17.700 --> 01:55:18.823
with subtitles on,

01:55:18.823 --> 01:55:21.090
because you either pay
attention to a Japanese

01:55:21.090 --> 01:55:22.204
or you read the subtitles.

01:55:22.204 --> 01:55:24.506
And it's really hard to
concentrate on doing both.

01:55:24.506 --> 01:55:26.752
And your mind, your mind works differently

01:55:26.752 --> 01:55:29.053
when it's just trying
to hear the language,

01:55:29.053 --> 01:55:30.708
as opposed to just reading the subtitles.

01:55:30.708 --> 01:55:31.541
- I think actually having

01:55:31.541 --> 01:55:33.345
the Japanese subtitles helps more.

01:55:33.345 --> 01:55:34.331
- I would say so as well.

01:55:34.331 --> 01:55:36.634
- You see the sentence
and recognize some kanji.

01:55:36.634 --> 01:55:39.724
- I reckon, you get a sentence,

01:55:39.724 --> 01:55:41.409
you watch it and you listen

01:55:41.409 --> 01:55:42.635
then you stop then you go back

01:55:42.635 --> 01:55:44.649
and you play it again and you read.

01:55:44.649 --> 01:55:46.745
- But the average anime
watcher is not gonna do that

01:55:46.745 --> 01:55:48.428
because they just want
to listen to the story.

01:55:48.428 --> 01:55:49.796
- So you got to study.

01:55:49.796 --> 01:55:51.818
- Because the trade off you have to do

01:55:51.818 --> 01:55:54.730
if you want to learn
Japanese by watching anime

01:55:54.730 --> 01:55:56.340
is just to not enjoy the anime.

01:55:56.340 --> 01:55:57.951
- Yes, yes, yes.

01:55:57.951 --> 01:55:59.929
- Which is the unfortunate part of it.

01:55:59.929 --> 01:56:01.203
And it's what I realized as well.

01:56:01.203 --> 01:56:02.759
- Do I want to ruin this thing?

01:56:02.759 --> 01:56:04.652
This one of the last escapes I have.

01:56:04.652 --> 01:56:07.240
- So I guess the only like
solace to that is just

01:56:07.240 --> 01:56:10.447
like use an anime that you
already know inside and out

01:56:10.447 --> 01:56:11.926
and then re-watch it again to be like,

01:56:11.926 --> 01:56:13.747
all right, I already know the story.

01:56:13.747 --> 01:56:15.394
I'm just gonna use it
as like study material.

01:56:15.394 --> 01:56:16.227
- That's a good idea.

01:56:16.227 --> 01:56:17.363
And you can take like foreign movies

01:56:17.363 --> 01:56:18.444
that have been dubbed as well.

01:56:18.444 --> 01:56:19.599
That's another good strategy.

01:56:19.599 --> 01:56:21.248
- Yeah, exactly.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:56:21.248 --> 01:56:24.716
So what anime are you
folks watching as well?

01:56:24.716 --> 01:56:25.825
- Well they know what we're watching.

01:56:25.825 --> 01:56:27.232
What are you watching?

01:56:27.232 --> 01:56:28.958
We never got to that.

01:56:28.958 --> 01:56:30.528
- What's your favorite anime?

01:56:30.528 --> 01:56:31.361
- Uh, uh.

01:56:33.669 --> 01:56:34.502
Hang on.

01:56:34.502 --> 01:56:35.808
Which one of those sentences
am I answering first?

01:56:35.808 --> 01:56:36.641
- What's your favorite anime?

01:56:36.641 --> 01:56:37.474
- Baccano.

01:56:37.474 --> 01:56:38.955
- Nice.

01:56:38.955 --> 01:56:40.598
- That's good choice.
- That's good taste.

01:56:40.598 --> 01:56:42.375
- That's a really good taste.

01:56:42.375 --> 01:56:43.483
Why you on a show called Trash Taste

01:56:43.483 --> 01:56:45.256
when you got great taste.

01:56:45.256 --> 01:56:47.485
- I dubbed Baccano.
- Did you?

01:56:47.485 --> 01:56:48.566
Well, when I lived in Hong Kong,

01:56:48.566 --> 01:56:49.959
one of my jobs there was I was a dubber.

01:56:49.959 --> 01:56:50.823
So we dubbed anime.

01:56:50.823 --> 01:56:53.967
- Wait, you're one of the
Hong Kong voices in Baccano?

01:56:53.967 --> 01:56:57.390
- Yes. There was a main,
one of the main kids,

01:56:57.390 --> 01:57:01.161
young handsome guy, Friel
or something was his name.

01:57:01.161 --> 01:57:03.401
- Friel, that sounds really familiar.

01:57:03.401 --> 01:57:04.234
- There's a scar?

01:57:04.234 --> 01:57:05.471
- No, it wasn't scar boy.

01:57:05.471 --> 01:57:06.304
- Jacuzzi?

01:57:06.304 --> 01:57:08.545
- Young handsome not Jacuzzi.

01:57:08.545 --> 01:57:09.492
It was one of the main kids.

01:57:09.492 --> 01:57:11.126
- Firo?
- Yes!

01:57:11.126 --> 01:57:12.491
Firo. I'm Firo.

01:57:12.491 --> 01:57:14.545
I'm the old Russian man who was doing

01:57:14.545 --> 01:57:15.378
all the reincarnation stuff.

01:57:15.378 --> 01:57:17.146
- No fucking way.
- Really?

01:57:17.146 --> 01:57:19.530
- Can I have a look at your resume.

01:57:19.530 --> 01:57:22.280
- Is this like on IMDB somewhere?

01:57:24.736 --> 01:57:28.270
- Ladybeard is a fucking
anime dub voice actor.

01:57:28.270 --> 01:57:30.958
- What the hell haven't you done?

01:57:30.958 --> 01:57:32.882
- This is so insane, that
it sounds like bullshit.

01:57:32.882 --> 01:57:35.342
- We did the English dubs for Animax.

01:57:35.342 --> 01:57:37.652
So like say you're in Hong
Kong or Singapore or something.

01:57:37.652 --> 01:57:39.221
You can watch Animax in three languages,

01:57:39.221 --> 01:57:42.511
Japanese, local language,
like Cantonese or English.

01:57:42.511 --> 01:57:44.977
So we did the English
dubs for Asia on Animax.

01:57:44.977 --> 01:57:47.451
- So that wouldn't be the
English dub that played-

01:57:47.451 --> 01:57:49.509
- On the DVD in America, no.

01:57:49.509 --> 01:57:50.577
It's amazing going to conventions

01:57:50.577 --> 01:57:52.890
and talking to American
dubbers cause they're like,

01:57:52.890 --> 01:57:55.972
yeah one episode we take
about five weeks to dub it.

01:57:55.972 --> 01:57:59.305
We were like, we did six episodes a day.

01:58:00.781 --> 01:58:02.964
Get them done. Get 'em done.

01:58:02.964 --> 01:58:06.693
- I have seen clips from
a lot of the English dubs

01:58:06.693 --> 01:58:09.360
for the English market.
- Animax.

01:58:10.729 --> 01:58:13.039
- You don't have time to mess around.

01:58:13.039 --> 01:58:16.539
But so I was, Tomozo in Chibi Maruko Chan.

01:58:17.603 --> 01:58:20.392
I was Nezumi Otoko in Gegege no Kitaro.

01:58:20.392 --> 01:58:21.547
- This is fucking insane.

01:58:21.547 --> 01:58:23.363
- I was Grelle in Black Butler.

01:58:23.363 --> 01:58:25.292
- You're Grelle in Black Butler?

01:58:25.292 --> 01:58:27.959
- I'm Grelle, I'm bloody Grelle.

01:58:28.928 --> 01:58:29.971
- What is going on?

01:58:29.971 --> 01:58:31.774
- If for Chinese listeners

01:58:31.774 --> 01:58:34.944
in Pleasant Goat and Big
Big Wolf, I was the wolf.

01:58:34.944 --> 01:58:35.813
You know that show?

01:58:35.813 --> 01:58:37.174
- You did it in Chinese?

01:58:37.174 --> 01:58:38.452
- No, we dubbed into English.

01:58:38.452 --> 01:58:40.236
But the original show is Chinese show.

01:58:40.236 --> 01:58:41.736
Big time in China.

01:58:43.502 --> 01:58:46.130
We did tons of it. We did Gundam Age.

01:58:46.130 --> 01:58:48.917
I was the flirty dude in Gundam Age,

01:58:48.917 --> 01:58:50.027
can't remember his name.

01:58:50.027 --> 01:58:51.354
Gundam Sangoku Soketsuden.

01:58:51.354 --> 01:58:53.661
- You must have really bashing these out.

01:58:53.661 --> 01:58:55.259
I don't know what the fuck
I did, I just turn up.

01:58:55.259 --> 01:58:56.942
- You do, you do. You show up,

01:58:56.942 --> 01:58:59.730
what is it? All right. The
thing. Okay. All right.

01:58:59.730 --> 01:59:00.563
Just knock them out.

01:59:00.563 --> 01:59:02.054
- Jesus.

01:59:02.054 --> 01:59:04.554
- So did you even know
who you were playing

01:59:04.554 --> 01:59:05.387
or the character as well?

01:59:05.387 --> 01:59:07.559
Or did you just turn up and
there was a script there

01:59:07.559 --> 01:59:08.500
and you just had to read?

01:59:08.500 --> 01:59:10.323
- Normally at the start of series

01:59:10.323 --> 01:59:13.108
we'd get to do a little bit of research.

01:59:13.108 --> 01:59:13.941
- And we get told, okay.

01:59:13.941 --> 01:59:15.283
Here's approximately what
happens in the story.

01:59:15.283 --> 01:59:17.005
Here's approximately
who your character is.

01:59:17.005 --> 01:59:18.357
And then we figure out the voice.

01:59:18.357 --> 01:59:19.190
We've said that with the director

01:59:19.190 --> 01:59:20.714
we figured out the
voice we're going to do.

01:59:20.714 --> 01:59:23.193
- No audition process?

01:59:23.193 --> 01:59:24.565
- No.

01:59:24.565 --> 01:59:27.587
Audition was to get hired by the studio.

01:59:27.587 --> 01:59:31.974
So you'd been hired and
now you good enough to do.

01:59:31.974 --> 01:59:34.101
But then we did like,
Inazuma Eleven, right?

01:59:34.101 --> 01:59:36.253
Cause there's so many
characters in that show.

01:59:36.253 --> 01:59:39.080
Everybody has like a hundred characters.

01:59:39.080 --> 01:59:41.226
So you kind of, you run
out of voices, right?

01:59:41.226 --> 01:59:43.321
The soccer teams, Cause
they rotate through

01:59:43.321 --> 01:59:44.756
and you remember a few episodes.

01:59:44.756 --> 01:59:47.459
You just, your team
from three episodes ago

01:59:47.459 --> 01:59:51.215
starts their voices become
the new teams voices.

01:59:51.215 --> 01:59:53.277
- Everyone's forced to
be Mel Brooks, basically.

01:59:53.277 --> 01:59:55.023
It's just like, let's do a hundred voices.

01:59:55.023 --> 01:59:55.976
Just pull them out.

01:59:55.976 --> 01:59:57.290
- Big time, that was a great job.

01:59:57.290 --> 01:59:58.926
But that was wiped out of
the financial crisis you see?

01:59:58.926 --> 01:59:59.759
- Oh jeez.

01:59:59.759 --> 02:00:01.442
- So I had a killer life before then.

02:00:01.442 --> 02:00:03.786
Stuntman, voice actor, that was dope.

02:00:03.786 --> 02:00:05.974
- I can't believe you're
an anime dub voice actor.

02:00:05.974 --> 02:00:07.814
- They say you're the Jack of all trades

02:00:07.814 --> 02:00:09.240
literally the embodiment.

02:00:09.240 --> 02:00:11.154
- You know Omni Productions?

02:00:11.154 --> 02:00:15.330
- Oh they have the funniest
transformers dub you have.

02:00:15.330 --> 02:00:16.163
- That's what they were famous for.

02:00:16.163 --> 02:00:17.614
- It's famous, because
this transformer dub

02:00:17.614 --> 02:00:21.144
is fucking awful. It is so fucking awful.

02:00:21.144 --> 02:00:24.463
- Is this the same company
that dubs Dragon Ball movies?

02:00:24.463 --> 02:00:26.154
- I think there is, it might be, but yeah.

02:00:26.154 --> 02:00:28.026
Omni dubs is like.
- Yeah.

02:00:28.026 --> 02:00:30.864
That's what they were notorious for.

02:00:30.864 --> 02:00:32.062
- There's like a Twitter account

02:00:32.062 --> 02:00:34.107
dedicated to just posting clips from it

02:00:34.107 --> 02:00:35.774
just out of context.

02:00:36.616 --> 02:00:38.184
- What's happened to the headmasters.

02:00:38.184 --> 02:00:40.675
Can't they fight without Chrome Dome?

02:00:40.675 --> 02:00:43.888
- I just showed the boys some
of the transformers dubs.

02:00:43.888 --> 02:00:44.924
- It's hilarious.

02:00:44.924 --> 02:00:48.454
- That was before my time at the company.

02:00:48.454 --> 02:00:50.875
- So did the quality
actually go up you know?

02:00:50.875 --> 02:00:54.022
- I don't know, it
depends on what you think.

02:00:54.022 --> 02:00:55.876
- Okay listen, when I'm
doing voice acting right,

02:00:55.876 --> 02:00:57.945
I know when I'm in a project
that's garbage right?

02:00:57.945 --> 02:00:59.376
- Of course. Cause you're
a voice actor too, yes.

02:00:59.376 --> 02:01:01.700
- I know when I'm in
something and I'm like,

02:01:01.700 --> 02:01:02.990
this is not going on the resume.

02:01:02.990 --> 02:01:04.591
You know what I mean? You can tell.

02:01:04.591 --> 02:01:06.176
Did you get that feeling
when you're doing any

02:01:06.176 --> 02:01:08.675
of these dubs or you're like,
this is like, this is okay.

02:01:08.675 --> 02:01:10.647
Or this is like, I don't
think this is good.

02:01:10.647 --> 02:01:12.031
Or you just like this would work?

02:01:12.031 --> 02:01:15.614
- Well, you know it's
like maybe sometimes,

02:01:17.067 --> 02:01:18.196
you gotta do what you gotta do.

02:01:18.196 --> 02:01:20.029
- I mean, I guess the fact
that we just found out

02:01:20.029 --> 02:01:22.523
that you used to be an anime
dub voice actor says something.

02:01:22.523 --> 02:01:26.496
- Yeah. But like, look there's
dubbing and there's dubbing.

02:01:26.496 --> 02:01:28.541
There's kind of stuff
that you get sent to do

02:01:28.541 --> 02:01:30.817
and it's some, you know, commercial thing

02:01:30.817 --> 02:01:33.788
and you know, the script is
written in broken English

02:01:33.788 --> 02:01:36.045
and you're just like, no, you just record.

02:01:36.045 --> 02:01:37.764
Okay. And you just do it.

02:01:37.764 --> 02:01:39.806
And then there's shows Black Butler,

02:01:39.806 --> 02:01:41.806
which were actual shows.

02:01:43.178 --> 02:01:46.100
Tell me about your voice acting life.

02:01:46.100 --> 02:01:51.100
- Just started when I was,
Oh my God. How old was I? 15?

02:01:51.412 --> 02:01:53.424
- Holy smokes.
- From like my room though.

02:01:53.424 --> 02:01:54.870
Like just doing it for
fun. Cause I loved it.

02:01:54.870 --> 02:01:56.161
- What, just doing like fan dubs?

02:01:56.161 --> 02:01:57.763
- Yeah. Just doing like anything.

02:01:57.763 --> 02:02:00.827
And then went to a start
doing that for awhile.

02:02:00.827 --> 02:02:01.660
Got better equipment.

02:02:01.660 --> 02:02:03.927
Had zero training for awhile.

02:02:03.927 --> 02:02:07.144
And then manage to got
some roles very luckily.

02:02:07.144 --> 02:02:09.101
Oh my God, one of the most
embarrassing ones is that

02:02:09.101 --> 02:02:11.490
I've voiced like, I couldn't do this now

02:02:11.490 --> 02:02:13.181
I think you know what I'm talking about?

02:02:13.181 --> 02:02:15.068
You're gonna fucking love it.

02:02:15.068 --> 02:02:17.029
So I voiced a Nigerian.

02:02:17.029 --> 02:02:19.854
- Oh dear, you can't do that.

02:02:19.854 --> 02:02:21.669
- So what happened was, is that,

02:02:21.669 --> 02:02:23.527
again I was like, I was
like 17 when I did this.

02:02:23.527 --> 02:02:25.403
It was like Age of Empires.

02:02:25.403 --> 02:02:26.783
I'm sure you know that game.

02:02:26.783 --> 02:02:28.646
They literally were doing a
competition when I was like

02:02:28.646 --> 02:02:29.760
you can voice in the game.

02:02:29.760 --> 02:02:31.927
And I was like, fantastic.

02:02:32.780 --> 02:02:35.193
So they wanted Nigerian accents.

02:02:35.193 --> 02:02:38.964
And so I quickly opened up
Google tab go to YouTube,

02:02:38.964 --> 02:02:40.955
Nigerian accent example.

02:02:40.955 --> 02:02:42.884
Listen to some guy who's Nigerian speaking

02:02:42.884 --> 02:02:46.111
and I was like, I'm pretty
sure I can get close to this.

02:02:46.111 --> 02:02:47.263
Submitted an audition.

02:02:47.263 --> 02:02:48.294
Didn't think anything of it.

02:02:48.294 --> 02:02:50.479
A year later at the like, yeah so,

02:02:50.479 --> 02:02:53.185
yeah, we used your lines
in the game, and I'm like.

02:02:53.185 --> 02:02:54.480
Can I re-record them?

02:02:54.480 --> 02:02:56.450
No, They're in the game.

02:02:56.450 --> 02:02:57.916
- The game came out yesterday.

02:02:57.916 --> 02:03:01.034
- It's out now. I'm like, What?

02:03:01.034 --> 02:03:03.027
But I didn't like sign
any contracts or anything.

02:03:03.027 --> 02:03:04.646
So I don't know.

02:03:04.646 --> 02:03:06.549
- Did you get paid for it or?

02:03:06.549 --> 02:03:08.551
- They paid me like 200
bucks. I'm like, thanks.

02:03:08.551 --> 02:03:10.729
Pat me on the back.
Like get him outta here.

02:03:10.729 --> 02:03:14.363
- I was gonna say, that's
called getting it done for free.

02:03:14.363 --> 02:03:17.903
- But like it was like it was
so long in between you know.

02:03:17.903 --> 02:03:20.024
- Is that legal?
- I don't know.

02:03:20.024 --> 02:03:21.532
- Can they just use your
voice without you signing?

02:03:21.532 --> 02:03:23.077
- It's a competition.
- I'm -

02:03:23.077 --> 02:03:24.834
I'm pretty sure when you
send in the competition,

02:03:24.834 --> 02:03:25.667
they you know.

02:03:25.667 --> 02:03:28.249
- The fine print probably
says something right? Yeah.

02:03:28.249 --> 02:03:29.082
- That's amazing.

02:03:29.082 --> 02:03:30.765
So you got into League
of Legends as a Nigerian.

02:03:30.765 --> 02:03:33.658
- No, sorry. Age of Empires.
- Age of Empires.

02:03:33.658 --> 02:03:37.390
- If Riot Games was
doing this, Jesus Christ.

02:03:37.390 --> 02:03:39.223
- Sorry, sorry, sorry.

02:03:40.423 --> 02:03:41.735
- I mean Riot Games did
redub one of their character.

02:03:41.735 --> 02:03:44.080
- Oy, they both have
alliteration in title.

02:03:44.080 --> 02:03:45.802
You can't blame me that much.

02:03:45.802 --> 02:03:48.884
- It was weird cause like, you know.

02:03:48.884 --> 02:03:53.168
I'm voicing some archer in some
DLC that like never appears.

02:03:53.168 --> 02:03:55.669
And my mate is obsessed
with Age of Empires,

02:03:55.669 --> 02:03:57.038
he just messaged me one day.

02:03:57.038 --> 02:03:59.046
He's like, I think I found you

02:03:59.046 --> 02:04:01.466
and he sends me an unlisted YouTube clip.

02:04:01.466 --> 02:04:02.468
And it's like, you know

02:04:02.468 --> 02:04:03.396
cause you know Age of Empires

02:04:03.396 --> 02:04:04.446
when you're moving around the wall

02:04:04.446 --> 02:04:05.986
It's like a dark circle
that comes visible.

02:04:05.986 --> 02:04:08.352
And there's the Nigerian
archer walks in and he's like,

02:04:08.352 --> 02:04:11.217
Hello. And welcome to the village.

02:04:11.217 --> 02:04:14.762
It's literally like the
Ugandan Knuckles meme,

02:04:14.762 --> 02:04:16.095
before the meme.

02:04:17.394 --> 02:04:18.708
I've shown clips of it before.

02:04:18.708 --> 02:04:21.043
Cause I just think it's so
fucking embarrassing and stupid.

02:04:21.043 --> 02:04:22.793
- Well that's not PC.

02:04:23.994 --> 02:04:25.464
- There's no way you could
get away with that today.

02:04:25.464 --> 02:04:28.234
- As questionable as it
was, But even in like 2015,

02:04:28.234 --> 02:04:31.433
that was, there was like
still no problem with that.

02:04:31.433 --> 02:04:32.427
- Internet was a different time.

02:04:32.427 --> 02:04:34.934
- There was never a source
of that being problematic.

02:04:34.934 --> 02:04:39.140
Now I would never dream of
auditioning for a Nigerian.

02:04:39.140 --> 02:04:40.758
- I mean, you're also
17 at that time right?

02:04:40.758 --> 02:04:42.575
- Yeah I was like a literal fucking child,

02:04:42.575 --> 02:04:44.345
I thought, I can be a Nigerian archer.

02:04:44.345 --> 02:04:46.487
- When I first did my like

02:04:46.487 --> 02:04:48.312
actor registry stuff in Australia,

02:04:48.312 --> 02:04:50.654
you have to list accents you can do.

02:04:50.654 --> 02:04:51.610
And I went through the
ones I thought I could do.

02:04:51.610 --> 02:04:53.869
- You just bullshit.

02:04:53.869 --> 02:04:55.088
- French or whatever.

02:04:55.088 --> 02:04:57.323
But then it comes over like Korean,

02:04:57.323 --> 02:04:58.602
yeah, I'll just do an impersonation

02:04:58.602 --> 02:05:00.160
of my TaeKwonDo master, tick.

02:05:00.160 --> 02:05:04.099
Japanese, just do a impersonation
of my friend Yuji, tick.

02:05:04.099 --> 02:05:08.796
Which is I would never, ever,
ever need to fricking voice.

02:05:08.796 --> 02:05:09.629
- Sorry I was doing that.

02:05:09.629 --> 02:05:10.578
And then yeah, it just came into a thing

02:05:10.578 --> 02:05:11.411
and start doing classes.

02:05:11.411 --> 02:05:12.809
Got workshops, got more experienced

02:05:12.809 --> 02:05:14.297
to professional work
at London for a while.

02:05:14.297 --> 02:05:15.138
It was pretty chill.

02:05:15.138 --> 02:05:18.931
- In London. So now,
you're voice acting here?

02:05:18.931 --> 02:05:21.506
- I have done some things here.

02:05:21.506 --> 02:05:23.118
The one thing we did, we
can't talk about it yet so.

02:05:23.118 --> 02:05:25.094
- Yeah, yeah. Connor and
I did something recently

02:05:25.094 --> 02:05:26.790
but we can't talk about it.

02:05:26.790 --> 02:05:27.989
- I don't think it's been recently,

02:05:27.989 --> 02:05:28.981
I remember you guys talking about it.

02:05:28.981 --> 02:05:32.012
- It was ages ago, but it
still hasn't been released.

02:05:32.012 --> 02:05:33.543
- Really? That happens a lot.

02:05:33.543 --> 02:05:34.376
- Yeah.

02:05:34.376 --> 02:05:35.436
- I shot a thing in 2016

02:05:35.436 --> 02:05:37.003
that came out like a few weeks ago.

02:05:37.003 --> 02:05:38.535
- What? Jesus Christ.

02:05:38.535 --> 02:05:39.411
- I feel like what you do,

02:05:39.411 --> 02:05:40.702
is you just record these things

02:05:40.702 --> 02:05:42.063
and then it's a pleasant surprise like,

02:05:42.063 --> 02:05:42.896
two, three years later.

02:05:42.896 --> 02:05:43.735
When it comes out-
- Just forget about it.

02:05:43.735 --> 02:05:45.519
- It's like, oh yeah, I did that.

02:05:45.519 --> 02:05:48.664
- Oh God, I want to redo all my lines.

02:05:48.664 --> 02:05:50.602
- Let's hope the world
hasn't changed around you

02:05:50.602 --> 02:05:52.010
too much in the time.

02:05:52.010 --> 02:05:52.843
- Yeah, I hope not.

02:05:52.843 --> 02:05:53.676
- You're not breaking
any laws by accident.

02:05:53.676 --> 02:05:57.812
- Hey guys, this is my
newest Nigerian role.

02:05:57.812 --> 02:06:00.206
I recorded that seven years ago.

02:06:00.206 --> 02:06:02.524
- Hope you like it.

02:06:02.524 --> 02:06:04.668
- Today at the voice of
Africa radio network.

02:06:04.668 --> 02:06:07.634
We would like you to meet
Nigerian voice actor, Connor.

02:06:07.634 --> 02:06:09.901
- Did you have to do
like an Afrikaans accent?

02:06:09.901 --> 02:06:12.249
Or did you have to like
ever put on an accent

02:06:12.249 --> 02:06:14.111
for any of the anime voices you had to do?

02:06:14.111 --> 02:06:14.944
- All the time.

02:06:14.944 --> 02:06:15.777
- All the time?

02:06:15.777 --> 02:06:16.610
- All the time.

02:06:16.610 --> 02:06:19.464
- Because I can't really imagine
like an Australian accent.

02:06:19.464 --> 02:06:21.334
- The problem with accents is that,

02:06:21.334 --> 02:06:23.188
you always think you're
better at doing them

02:06:23.188 --> 02:06:24.896
than you actually are.

02:06:24.896 --> 02:06:26.379
Because you know, even
if you're very good,

02:06:26.379 --> 02:06:27.864
a native will be able to pick it apart.

02:06:27.864 --> 02:06:28.763
And they'll be like.

02:06:28.763 --> 02:06:30.061
- Because when I did the,

02:06:30.061 --> 02:06:32.702
I did a voice for Pop Team Epic

02:06:32.702 --> 02:06:34.951
but like the character was-
- American.

02:06:34.951 --> 02:06:36.951
- An American.

02:06:36.951 --> 02:06:39.687
It was the mayor of New
York right? In the story.

02:06:39.687 --> 02:06:43.374
(everyone laughing)

02:06:43.374 --> 02:06:45.195
It was literally the mayor of New York.

02:06:45.195 --> 02:06:46.028
And I was like,

02:06:46.028 --> 02:06:48.046
and I said to the director
in Japanese I was like,

02:06:48.046 --> 02:06:50.152
so do I have to like do
it in an American accent?

02:06:50.152 --> 02:06:52.310
Like I can do an American
accent, but it's not great.

02:06:52.310 --> 02:06:53.270
Like I'm just letting you know.

02:06:53.270 --> 02:06:55.545
And he's like, no, just fucking say it.

02:06:55.545 --> 02:06:57.545
And I'm like, all right.

02:07:00.051 --> 02:07:01.032
So I was like okay,

02:07:01.032 --> 02:07:03.555
I need to see like how
far the limit is right?

02:07:03.555 --> 02:07:05.624
Because usually they don't
take the first take right?

02:07:05.624 --> 02:07:08.503
So I can just kind of,
test the limits to see like

02:07:08.503 --> 02:07:11.953
how far I can go before I have
to eventually redo it again.

02:07:11.953 --> 02:07:13.998
So my first take was dead ass like,

02:07:13.998 --> 02:07:17.961
I am the mayor of New York
and yeah, welcome everybody.

02:07:17.961 --> 02:07:19.240
And they fucking took it.

02:07:19.240 --> 02:07:21.928
- Well cause they don't know.
